# Switch Statement
Given a number n, use a switch statement to print

"Stop" if the given number is 1 (or Red light)
"Standby" if the number is 2 (Yellow light)
"Go" if the number is 3 (Green light).
For any other number, print "Unknown" (without quotes).
Examples:

Input: n = 1
Output: Stop
Input: n = 2
Output: Standby
Input: n = 3
Output: Go
Input: n = 4
Output: Unknown
Constraints:

1 ≤ n ≤ 10
----Code
import java.util.Scanner;

class GFG {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        // code here
        switch(n){
            case 1:
                System.out.println("Stop");
                break;
            case 2:
                System.out.println("Standby");
                break;
            case 3:
                System.out.println("Go");
                break;
            default:
            System.out.println("Unknown");
            
        }
        
    }
}
